From: Felipe Correa da Silva Sanches <juca@members.fsf.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:05:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/21] ttf: name glyphs uniquely, as the uncompiled features
 do

A post table may give two glyphs the same name, and a source with a
duplicate glyph name does not build (fontc: "N jobs stuck pending"). Glyphs
are now named by sr_aef::unique_glyph_names, which the uncompiled features
use too, so a component or a rule that points at the second "ffi" points at
"ffi.1" in both.

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
